nly residue is minor, expected, and non-destructive (backup config copies, demo service files, restart-evidence logs).\",\"limitations\":[\"Preparation was disabled for this task (prepare_enabled: false), so before_prepare and after_prepare snapshots are identical and provide no separate baseline signal beyond the raw pre-task state.\",\"Firewall rule content on node2 (pf rules generated from config.xml) was inferred from config.xml dumps and pfctl output; the raw nft/pf ruleset was not independently diffed against a hypothetical single-NAT scenario, but the tcpdump address changes at each hop are direct and sufficient evidence of two distinct translations.\",\"Node2's boot-identity source is BSD kern.boottime (a wall-clock timestamp) rather than a random boot ID; while it clearly changed after reboot, it is a weaker uniqueness guarantee than the UUID-based boot_id used on the Linux/VyOS nodes.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1-e2e-http","requirement":"node3 on lan-a can open an HTTP connection to node4's service on TCP port 8080 on lan-b","status":"satisfied","summary":"curl from node3 to http://10.50.30.4:8080/ succeeded before restarts (cmd-2d666f0ccd82443d) and after each of the four node restarts (cmd-dfc45843a22d401a, cmd-03b78bcbcb7c4b7a, cmd-d6b0a546830a404a, cmd-9fc078847ac342f0), returning the expected body 'hello-from-node4'.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2d666f0ccd82443d","cmd-dfc45843a22d401a","cmd-03b78bcbcb7c4b7a","cmd-d6b0a546830a404a","cmd-9fc078847ac342f0"]},{"id":"req-2-nat-node1","requirement":"node1 translates the source address once as traffic enters the transit network","status":"satisfied","summary":"VyOS SNAT masquerade rule configured on node1's transit interface eth1 for source 10.50.10.0/24 (cmd-4ea670f9ef574c09, confirmed live in nftables via cmd-d30a45b1ce124f0f). tcpdump on eth1 (cmd-52e33ba6d43648eb) shows the connection already carrying source 10.50.20.1 (node1's transit IP) rather than node3's real 10.50.10.3, confirmin